The operating system's name, given to configure

configure writes PHP_OS, which the constant PHP_OS gives at run time,
from the build machine's uname. In a cross build that is not the system
PHP runs on: a PHP built on Linux for Dukovo would say it runs on Linux,
and the tests of PHP's suite that are for Linux alone would run on it.
configure takes PHP_UNAME from the environment already; this lets it
take PHP_OS, with uname's output still the default.

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 359f22c2..0916b65d 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1423,7 +1423,9 @@ AC_ARG_VAR([PHP_UNAME],
 AS_VAR_IF([PHP_UNAME],, [PHP_UNAME=$(uname -a | xargs)])
 AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED([PHP_UNAME], ["$PHP_UNAME"], [The 'uname -a' output.])
 
-PHP_OS=$(uname | xargs)
+AC_ARG_VAR([PHP_OS],
+  [Operating system name (defaults to the 'uname' output)])
+AS_VAR_IF([PHP_OS],, [PHP_OS=$(uname | xargs)])
 AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED([PHP_OS], ["$PHP_OS"], [The 'uname' output.])
 
 AC_ARG_VAR([PHP_BUILD_SYSTEM],
